WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610 align:middle line:90%


00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.900 align:middle line:84%
PROFESSOR: So in
quantum mechanics,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.030 align:middle line:84%
you see this i appearing here,
and it's a complex number--

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.030 align:middle line:90%
the square root of minus 1.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.390 align:middle line:84%
And that shows that
somehow complex numbers

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.530 align:middle line:90%
are very important.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.160 align:middle line:84%
Well it's difficult
to overemphasize

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.810 align:middle line:90%
the importance of i--

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:32.299 align:middle line:84%
is the square root of minus 1
was invented by people in order

00:00:32.299 --> 00:00:33.950 align:middle line:90%
to solve equations.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.735 align:middle line:84%
Equations like x
squared equals minus 1.

00:00:38.735 --> 00:00:42.150 align:middle line:84%
And it so happens
that once you invent i

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.100 align:middle line:84%
you need to invent
more numbers, and you

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.070 align:middle line:84%
can solve every polynomial
equation with just i.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.660 align:middle line:84%
And square root of i--
well square root of i

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.340 align:middle line:84%
can be written in terms
of i and other numbers.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:02.980 align:middle line:84%
So if you have a
complex number z--

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.040 align:middle line:84%
we sometimes write
it this way, and we

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.670 align:middle line:84%
say it belongs to
the complex numbers,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.450 align:middle line:84%
and with a and b belonging
to the real numbers.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.260 align:middle line:84%
And we say that
the real part of z

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:23.770 align:middle line:84%
is a, the imaginary
part of z is b.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.520 align:middle line:84%
We also define the
complex conjugate of z,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:37.090 align:middle line:84%
which is a minus i b and we
picture the complex number z

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:42.040 align:middle line:84%
by putting a on the
x-axis b on the y-axis,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.720 align:middle line:84%
and we think of the
complex number z here--

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.670 align:middle line:84%
kind of like putting
the real numbers here

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.790 align:middle line:90%
and the imaginary parts here.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:56.140 align:middle line:84%
So you can think
of this as ib or b,

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.800 align:middle line:84%
but this is the complex number--
maybe ib would be a better way

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.110 align:middle line:90%
to write it here.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:09.110 align:middle line:84%
So with complex numbers, there
is one more useful identity.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:13.100 align:middle line:84%
You define the norm
of the complex number

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:17.870 align:middle line:84%
to be square root of a
squared plus b squared

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.410 align:middle line:84%
and then this
results in the norm

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.700 align:middle line:84%
squared being a
squared plus b squared.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.230 align:middle line:84%
And it's actually equal
to z times z star.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.940 align:middle line:90%
A very fundamental equation--

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.640 align:middle line:90%
z times z star--

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.170 align:middle line:84%
if you multiply z
times z star, you

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.940 align:middle line:90%
get a squared plus b squared.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:43.340 align:middle line:90%
So the norm squared--

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.830 align:middle line:84%
the norm of this thing
is a real number.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.160 align:middle line:90%


00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.020 align:middle line:90%
And that's pretty important.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:03:01.320 align:middle line:84%
So there is one other
identity that is very useful

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.590 align:middle line:84%
and I might well
mention it here as we're

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:08.010 align:middle line:84%
going to be working
with complex numbers.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.250 align:middle line:84%
And for more practice
on complex numbers,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.070 align:middle line:90%
you'll see the homework.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:22.460 align:middle line:84%
So suppose I have in the
complex plane an angle theta,

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.910 align:middle line:84%
and I want to figure out what
is this complex number z here

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.620 align:middle line:90%
at unit radius.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:37.290 align:middle line:84%
So I would know that it's real
part would be cosine theta.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.736 align:middle line:90%


00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:45.220 align:middle line:84%
And its imaginary part
would be sine theta.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.480 align:middle line:90%
It's a circle of radius 1.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.240 align:middle line:90%


00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.780 align:middle line:84%
So that must be
the complex number.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:59.880 align:middle line:84%
z must be equal to cosine
theta plus i sine theta.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.350 align:middle line:84%
Because the real part
of it is cosine theta.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:07.790 align:middle line:84%
It's in that horizontal
part's projection.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:12.440 align:middle line:84%
And the imaginary part is
the vertical projection.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.110 align:middle line:84%
Well the thing that
is very amazing

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:20.060 align:middle line:84%
is that this is equal
to e to the i theta.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.480 align:middle line:90%
And that is very non-trivial.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.150 align:middle line:84%
To prove it, you
have to work a bit,

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.030 align:middle line:84%
but it's a very famous
result and we'll use it.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.420 align:middle line:90%


00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:35.970 align:middle line:90%
So that is complex numbers.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:42.690 align:middle line:84%
So complex numbers you use
them in electromagnetism.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.750 align:middle line:84%
You sometimes use them
in classical mechanics,

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.200 align:middle line:84%
but you always use it
in an auxiliary way.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:55.440 align:middle line:84%
It was not directly relevant
because the electric field

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.430 align:middle line:84%
is real, the position is,
real the velocity is real--

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.030 align:middle line:84%
everything is real and
the equations are real.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.820 align:middle line:84%
On the other hand,
in quantum mechanics,

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.820 align:middle line:90%
the equation already has an i.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:19.500 align:middle line:84%
So in quantum mechanics, psi is
a complex number necessarily.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.470 align:middle line:90%
It has to be.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:27.620 align:middle line:84%
In fact, if it would be real,
you would have a contradiction

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.410 align:middle line:84%
because if psi is
real, turns out

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:36.410 align:middle line:84%
for all physical systems we're
interested in, H on psi real

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.930 align:middle line:90%
gives you a real thing.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.490 align:middle line:84%
And here, if psi is real
then the relative is real,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.030 align:middle line:84%
and this is imaginary and
you have a contradiction.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:48.830 align:middle line:84%
So there are no
solutions that are real.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.890 align:middle line:90%
So you need complex numbers.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.750 align:middle line:90%
They're not auxiliary.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:57.420 align:middle line:84%
On the other hand, you can
never measure a complex number.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.600 align:middle line:90%
You measure real numbers--

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.780 align:middle line:84%
ammeter, position,
weight, anything

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.030 align:middle line:84%
that you really measure
at the end of the day

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.690 align:middle line:90%
is a real number.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:11.190 align:middle line:84%
So if the wave function
was a complex number,

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.310 align:middle line:84%
it was the issue of what is
the physical interpretation.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.910 align:middle line:84%
And Max Born had
the idea that you

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.660 align:middle line:84%
have to calculate the
real number called

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.360 align:middle line:84%
the norm of this
square, and this is

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.240 align:middle line:90%
proportional to probabilities.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:33.040 align:middle line:90%


00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.810 align:middle line:84%
So that was a great
discovery and had a lot

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.460 align:middle line:84%
to do with the development
of quantum mechanics.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.850 align:middle line:90%
Many people hated this.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.420 align:middle line:84%
In fact, Schrodinger
himself hated it,

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:50.440 align:middle line:84%
and his invention of
the Schrodinger cat

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.630 align:middle line:84%
was an attempt to
show how ridiculous

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:56.470 align:middle line:84%
was the idea of thinking of
these things as probabilities.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.490 align:middle line:84%
But he was wrong, and Einstein
was wrong in that way.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:05.260 align:middle line:84%
But when very good
physicists are wrong,

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:08.050 align:middle line:84%
they are not wrong
for silly reasons,

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:11.140 align:middle line:84%
they are wrong for good
reasons, and we can learn a lot

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.820 align:middle line:90%
from their thinking.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.300 align:middle line:84%
And this EPR are
things that we will

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:21.640 align:middle line:84%
discuss at some moment in
your quantum sequence at MIT.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:25.090 align:middle line:84%
Einstein-Podolski-Rosen
was an attempt

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.280 align:middle line:84%
to show that quantum
mechanics was wrong

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.250 align:middle line:90%
and led to amazing discoveries.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:34.070 align:middle line:84%
It was the EPR paper
itself was wrong,

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:37.300 align:middle line:84%
but it brought up
ideas that turned out

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.120 align:middle line:90%
to be very important.